  "response_text": "A system call is a specific way that the user asks for a function call to be preformed. Since user programs shouldn\u2019t have access to everything they user system calls to ask the kernel to do something, like reading or writing. So to read or write data the program has to request that information from the OS through a system call. Then the os checks if the program should have access to that and then if it should it uses the kernel to get or write that information.\\n",
